{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And every saddle.</b> Even though he did not sit upon it — for instance, the saddle-pad of a riding-beast, which they call ארצו\"ן, is impure by reason of 'saddle'; and the riding-seat they call סל\"ויש is impure with the impurity of a seat (Eruvin 27)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {0 "ארצו\"ן likely corresponds to Old French arçon, 'pommel/saddle-bow'; סל\"ויש likely corresponds to Old French selois or similar, denoting a type of riding-seat or saddle."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:06:35.578736422Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}